From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:43:03 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ngp-flash

Beetle NeoPop gives slot no save RAM: it writes its own <stem>.flash
into its save dir only when the game unloads, truncating the file in
place, and trusts the lengths in the file it reads back. So the NGP
core now gets Saves/NGP/.core as its save dir (every other core keeps
Saves/), and slot moves the file between that staging dir and
Saves/NGP/<stem>.flash itself.

Before the core loads, the staged copy is cleared and the published file
is copied in only if it passes NeoPop's own layout: id 0x0053, at most
256 blocks, total_file_length equal to the file size, and every block
header and its data inside the file (mednafen/ngp/flash.c at a50d5ac,
flash_read and do_flash_read). A file that fails is renamed to
<stem>.flash-refused and logged, and the game starts with blank flash. An
old Saves/<stem>.flash from before this patch is moved into Saves/NGP/
once.

Lid close, POWER, battery critical, the 60 s autosave and eject already
ask the core for its save RAM; for NGP that request now flushes by
reload on the emu thread (serialize, load the cart again so the core
writes its flash, unserialize) and the game carries on. After every
flush and after the core is dropped, a staged file that passes the check
and differs from the published one is published with the atomic writer
(temp file, fsync, rename), so a torn write never reaches the final path.
The reload took 0.12 ms on the M5 Max. If the reload fails, the core is
stopped and the resume state, which carries the flash, is the copy.
